.TH JITTERENTROPY-RNG 1 2026-09-30 "jitterentropy x.y.z" "User Commands"
.\" groff re-enables hyphenation per paragraph unless HY is 0.
.nr HY 0
.nh
.SH NAME
jitterentropy-rng \- generate random data with the CPU Jitter RNG
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jitterentropy-rng
.I blocks
.RI [ option " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jitterentropy-rng
initializes the CPU Jitter Random Number Generator, allocates one entropy
collector and writes
.I blocks
blocks of 32 bytes of its output to standard output. The data are the
conditioned output of the Jitter RNG, as
.BR jent_read_entropy_safe ()
of
.BR jent_read_entropy (3)
delivers them; the raw time deltas of the noise source are recorded with
.BR jitterentropy-hashtime (1).
.PP
The status document of the collector, as
.BR jent_status (3)
writes it, is printed to standard error before the first block. In FIPS or
NTG.1 mode the health test failures are reported there as well, the
intermittent ones the read recovers from included.
.SH OPTIONS
The first eight options set the
.B JENT_*
flag of the same name or field, described in
.BR jent_entropy_collector_alloc (3).
Options are matched by their prefix.
.TP
.B \-\-ntg1
AIS 20/31 NTG.1 compliant operation
.RB ( JENT_NTG1 ).
.TP
.B \-\-force\-fips
FIPS 140 and SP800-90B compliant operation
.RB ( JENT_FORCE_FIPS ).
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-memory\-access
No memory access noise source
.RB ( JENT_DISABLE_MEMORY_ACCESS ).
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-internal\-timer
Never use the internal timer
.RB ( JENT_DISABLE_INTERNAL_TIMER ).
.TP
.B \-\-force\-internal\-timer
Use the internal timer instead of the hardware time stamp
.RB ( JENT_FORCE_INTERNAL_TIMER ).
.TP
.B \-\-all\-caches
Size the memory access region from all data caches
.RB ( JENT_CACHE_ALL ).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-mem " n"
Set the memory access region to 2^(\fIn\fR+9) bytes, with
.I n
from 1 (1 kB) to 20 (512 MB); 0 leaves the size to the library.
.TP
.BI \-\-hloopcnt " n"
Run 2^\fIn\fR hash loop iterations per measurement, with
.I n
from 0 to 7.
.TP
.BI \-\-osr " osr"
The oversampling rate; 0, the default, selects the minimum of 3.
.TP
.B \-\-hex
Write the blocks as hexadecimal digits instead of binary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when all blocks were written. When the initialization fails, the exit
status is the error code of
.BR jent_entropy_init_ex ()
of
.BR jent_entropy_init (3).
Any other failure - an invalid argument, no collector, a failed read or
write - exits with 1.
.SH EXAMPLES
One megabyte of output for an assessment, the status kept aside:
.PP
.EX
jitterentropy-rng 32768 > output.bin 2> status.json
.EE
.PP
32 bytes in NTG.1 mode, printed as hexadecimal digits:
.PP
.EX
jitterentropy-rng 1 \-\-ntg1 \-\-hex
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jitterentropy-hashtime (1),
.BR jitterentropy-flags (1),
.BR jitterentropy-osr (1),
.BR jent_entropy_collector_alloc (3),
.BR jent_read_entropy (3),
.BR jent_status (3),
.BR jitterentropy (3)
